# Party banter at Argynvostholt and on the knights' road. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the node is eligible only
# while its condition holds. Party members speak only through interjections; a line plays if a matching member is
# present.

~ banter_patrol
if flag.order_patrol_met and not visited:argynvostholt
interject tag:blunt: Dead men keeping a road. Polite dead men. That's new.
interject class:wizard: Revenants, almost certainly. They don't rest until their vengeance is done. One wonders on whom.
endif
-> END

~ banter_patrol_order
if flag.order_patrol_met and not visited:argynvostholt and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Knights of the Silver Dragon! The real Order. I've carried Sir Aldric's sword all this way, Wren, and there they were.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Big man. They weren't breathing.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I noticed. I'll ask about it at the house. Politely.
endif
-> END

~ banter_ridge
if visited:argynvostholt and not flag.vladimir_met and name:wren_featherfoot and name:ratatoille
interject name:wren_featherfoot: A dragon's house. Dragons sleep on gold. I'm not saying anything. I'm just walking a bit faster.
interject name:ratatoille: Silver dragons, I'll have you know, hoarded people, not gold. Knights. Friends. Good company at table.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: So that's his hoard out on the road, then. Not breathing.
endif
-> END

~ banter_forty
if flag.vladimir_met and not flag.order_fate and name:thistle and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:thistle: Forty dead men on his chain. Grandda says a dog chained long enough forgets it's chained.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I'd still like to sit at that table with them. Just once. Is that daft?
interject name:thistle: No. Daft's when you stop wanting things.
endif
-> END

~ banter_godfrey
if flag.godfrey_met and not flag.godfrey_remembers and not guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym
interject tag:cheerful: I like Sir Godfrey. He's the only dead person in Barovia who's apologised to me.
interject tag:blunt: He's forgetting himself. Literally. Somebody should help with that before there's nothing left to help.
endif
-> END

~ banter_skull
if flag.argynvost_skull_known and not flag.argynvost_beacon_lit and name:kip_smudgewick and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:kip_smudgewick: So we break into a vampire's castle and take a dragon's head off his wall. Recovery of property. Strictly legal. Mostly.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Right then! I'll carry it. It'll be heavy, a dragon's head.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: That's your worry? Not the vampire? The weight?
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I'm good at heavy.
endif
-> END

~ banter_flame
if flag.dragon_fire_kindled and not flag.argynvost_beacon_lit and name:ratatoille and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:ratatoille: It isn't burning the torch. It isn't burning anything. It's not a fire at all. It's a fire remembering itself.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I was sent here to carry a light. I didn't know it would be a borrowed one. I'll carry it carefully.
endif
-> END

~ banter_lit
if flag.argynvost_beacon_lit and name:thistle and name:ratatoille
interject name:thistle: Look at it! Every farm in the valley can see that. Somebody's opening a shutter right now. Bet my boots.
interject name:ratatoille: So, I would point out, can the castle.
interject name:thistle: Good. Let him lie awake. Do vampires lie awake? Let him start.
endif
-> END

~ banter_march
if flag.order_fate == "ride"
interject tag:veteran: Dead knights for allies. They don't eat, they don't sleep, they don't desert. Every quartermaster's dream.
interject tag:curious: Do they get paid?
interject tag:veteran: In the only coin they want. Him.
endif
-> END

~ banter_pact
if flag.vladimir_pact and not flag.vladimir_pact_broken and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: He filled this valley with graves, and we swore to leave him living. The words sat in my mouth like stones.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: I know that one. You sign, it's done, and after that you carry it about in your chest.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Is that how it is for you, Kip?
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Most days. Apricot? They don't help. Have one anyway.
endif
-> END

~ banter_pact_broken
if flag.vladimir_pact_broken and name:wren_featherfoot and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:wren_featherfoot: We broke our word to a dead man. Master Sorrel would have something to say about that.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: What would he say?
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Don't know. That's the trouble with dead masters. You have to guess, and you always guess the hard one.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Then guess kindly. You broke a bad oath to keep a better one.
endif
-> END

~ banter_godfrey_guest
if guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: I've written all your names on the inside of my gauntlet. In case. You don't mind?
interject tag:cheerful: Put me down as the handsome one.
interject guest:sir_godfrey_gwilym: I'll put you down as the one who asked.
endif
-> END

~ banter_hunt
if flag.knights_hunt_seen
interject tag:blunt: They put down one of his messengers on the road and didn't even ask us first. I like them better every day.
endif
-> END

~ banter_beacon_road
if flag.beacon_light_seen
interject class:cleric: Every time we crest a hill, there it is. Somebody left a lamp in the window for us, long ago. We only lit it.
interject tag:curious: Do you think they knew we'd come?
endif
-> END
